stallion: DWC_usb31 USB Ethernet + live log (ADT /sweet-usb)

Runs the sweet USB stack of 0072-0077 (DWC3 device mode, ep0, CDC-ECM
ue0 192.168.7.2, UDP live log to 192.168.7.1:5140) on the Pixel 10a
"stallion" (DWC_usb31 1.30a at 0x11210000), with XNU started from Linux
(sweetjump) so PHY/repeater/VBUS/clocks/power are already up.

- Board selection at run time from the ADT: node /sweet-usb
  (tools/mkadt.py --target stallion) with reg = <u64 phys, u64 size> and
  optional sweet-sysmmu-ctrl = <u64 phys of the SysMMU CTRL_VM(0)>.
  Sweet's ADT has no such node: the Qualcomm path (GCC/QUSB2 probe,
  QSCRATCH VBUS override, plain CSFTRST) is unchanged.
- DWC_usb31 take-over as shim/usblog.c (worked on the phone): stop
  Linux's running session, SysMMU CTRL_VM(0) bit 0 off (bypass), GCTL
  device role, DCTL.CSFTRST with Linux's global registers snapshotted and
  restored, 50 ms + 100 ms settle; GUSB2PHYCFG0 SUSPHY/ENBLSLPM cleared
  around every endpoint command (serialized by a mutex); XferNotReady
  status phase decoded as (status & 3); the DMA area is cleaned once
  before use. No Qualcomm GCC/GDSC/QUSB2/QSCRATCH access on stallion.
- Started once from IOFindBSDRoot (before the root device lookup, so it
  does not depend on a UFS root) or from sweet_usb_probe(), whichever
  comes first. sweetusb defaults to 2 (gadget) on /sweet-usb boards;
  sweetusb=0 off, 1 register dump only; sweetusblog=0 as before.

